  "hints": [
    "You can postpone a chosen letter only if it appears again later.",
    "Maintain a stack and each letter's last position. A smaller incoming letter may replace a larger stack top that can still be recovered.",
    "Skip used letters. While top > current and last[top] > index, pop and unmark top; then push and mark current.",
    "Every removal improves the earliest differing position while preserving the ability to include all letters. Each occurrence is pushed and popped at most once."
  ],
  "editorial": "The stack holds the best feasible prefix. When a smaller unused letter arrives, remove larger trailing letters only if they occur later; otherwise removing them would lose a required letter. Greedy exchange at the first differing position justifies each pop. Skipping letters already retained prevents duplicates. The oracle enumerates all subsequences with exactly the required number of letters and selects the smallest containing the whole distinct alphabet.",
